<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vikramaditya I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 655–<a href="/years/680">680</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vikramaditya I was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badami">Badami</a> from about 655 to 680, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pulakeshin-ii">Pulakeshin II</a>. After the Pallavas had captured Badami in 642 and the kingdom fell into disorder, he expelled them, reunited the Chalukya lands and later raided the Pallava capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>. His successors kept the dynasty dominant in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> until 753.</p></div>
